  "narrative": "This exploration extends the independently validated dataset-only associations into lineage, technical, co-deletion, and biologically motivated context strata rather than adding weak marginal probes. For MDM2, H140 is validated and several strata support a CDKN2A-loss association, especially in TP53-wildtype cells, but the main untested high-value contexts are non-Avana library screens, lineage subgroups, and whether the association survives when MTAP is co-lost. The MDM2 CDKN2A-loss versus intact comparison within TP53-wildtype adenocarcinoma and squamous lines tests whether the effect is general across the two available lung histologic categories. The TP53-wildtype non-Avana test is the most important technical-robustness complement to the accepted Avana stratum. The TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss stratum tests whether the CDKN2A effect is specific to MTAP-intact cells or more broadly reflects a 9p21 co-deletion phenotype. For STAT3, H17 is validated overall and H121 supports a positive PTEN effect in TP53-loss cells; H163 is the data-driven reversed PTEN-by-TP53 interaction and remains active. I therefore register the direct PTEN effect among TP53-wildtype cells as a simpler and more interpretable complement to H163. If the PTEN effect is strong in TP53-wildtype cells, that would be consistent with a broad PTEN-loss association and would make any interaction attenuation less consequential. If it is weak or imprecise while the TP53-loss stratum is accepted, that would be more consistent with possible p53-dependent modification. For NFE2L2, H20 is validated and H68 supports the KEAP1-loss effect in STK11-loss cells; I register the STK11-intact stratum to test whether the KEAP1 association is independent of STK11 loss or whether STK11 co-occurrence is important. Expected signed estimates are positive for all proposed hypotheses, with a stronger expected MDM2/STAT3 effect and a strong expected NFE2L2 effect if the associations generalize within this dataset. Approximate 10 percent thresholds are about 0.027 MDM2 units, 0.028 STAT3 units, and 0.009 NFE2L2 units, so accepted effects far exceed these benchmarks and lower confidence bounds above threshold would support robustness within the supplied dataset. Wide intervals including null or both directions would remain unresolved, especially for sparse lineage or library strata. I keep H163 as the preferred validation candidate because it tests a potentially meaningful modest attenuation of the PTEN-STAT3 association in TP53-loss cells; the new direct TP53-wildtype comparison will help interpret the result if validation is available. All proposed comparisons are observational dataset-only hypotheses, not causal claims or claims of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 plan. Accepted validated core: SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency; PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency; TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency; CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2 dependency, strongest in TP53-wildtype. H163 active is top validation candidate for reversed STAT3 PTEN-by-TP53 interaction. New registered follow-ups: MDM2 CDKN2A loss among TP53-wildtype adenocarcinoma/squamous, TP53-wildtype non-Avana, and TP53-wildtype MTAP-loss; STAT3 PTEN loss among TP53-wildtype cells; NFE2L2 KEAP1 loss among STK11-intact cells. Next analysis priorities should be H163 if validation is being considered, existing accepted-effect robustness claims H76/H78/H79 for USP7 TP53, H80/H81/H82/H83/H84/H85/H60/H61 for lineage strata, H28 WRN non-Avana, and the new MDM2 and STAT3/NFE2L2 strata. Avoid further sparse technical interactions unless they are direct robustness strata. Do not accept lineage or library results unless interval is reasonably tight and effect exceeds approximate 10 percent threshold. All conclusions remain dataset-only and observational."
}

