  "narrative": "I registered new, falsifiable follow-ups focused on three themes: (1) new biologically motivated main predictors for outcomes where related pathways are already implicated, (2) low-growth robustness of the strongest validated dataset-only associations, and (3) a small number of pathway and technical strata that test whether accepted effects are context-dependent. STK11/LKB1 loss and ARID1A loss are plausible activators of stress/inflammatory signaling, including STAT3-associated programs; for these two hypotheses, direction -1 means stronger dependency is expected in the loss group, so a positive signed estimate would support the claim. RB1 loss is also plausible for stronger WRN dependency because RB1 loss can drive E2F-dependent replication stress; WRN resolves replication stress, so direction -1 again tests stronger dependency with loss. The low-growth comparisons split at 0.6 doublings per day and complement accepted high-growth strata for SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, KEAP1-NFE2L2, CDKN2A-MDM2 in TP53-wildtype cells, PTEN-STAT3, and TP53-USP7. These are not intended as new causal claims; they ask whether the magnitude remains clinically meaningful in slower-growing cells. For NFE2L2 and USP7 the accepted directions are weaker dependency (positive raw difference), so direction +1 is registered. PTEN loss within PIK3CA-mutant cells tests whether PTEN-STAT3 dependency remains strong when the PI3K pathway is activated by an alternative driver. Low-Cas9 strata for SMARCA2 and MDM2 provide technical robustness checks alongside accepted high-Cas9/Avana results, though intervals may be wider. Approximate 10-percent benchmarks are about 0.028 STAT3 units, 0.030 WRN units, 0.042 SMARCA2 units, 0.009 NFE2L2 units, 0.027 MDM2 units, and 0.018 USP7 units; signed estimates with lower confidence bounds above these values would support robust associations within this dataset. All proposals remain observational dataset-only associations and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 explore plan. Retain the six validated dataset-only associations: SMARCA4 loss-SMARCA2, MSI-high-WRN, KEAP1 loss-NFE2L2, PTEN loss-STAT3, TP53 loss-USP7, and CDKN2A loss-MDM2 in TP53-wildtype cells. Register 12 new analyses: STK11 loss and ARID1A loss as STAT3 predictors; RB1 loss as WRN predictor; low-growth robustness for SMARCA2, WRN, NFE2L2, TP53-wt MDM2, STAT3, and USP7; PTEN within PIK3CA-mutant STAT3; low-Cas9 for SMARCA2 and TP53-wt MDM2. Do not reopen rejected driver/marker claims unless new strong evidence emerges. Interpret estimates as signed to registered direction and compare with approximate 10-percent outcome-scale thresholds. Keep all conclusions dataset-only and non-causal."
}

