  "narrative": "All returned estimates are signed to the registered direction, so positive values support the registered hypothesis and negative values oppose it. I used approximate outcome-scale 10% benchmarks from the absolute means of each dependency outcome: about 0.028 for STAT3, 0.030 for WRN, 0.042 for SMARCA2, 0.009 for NFE2L2, 0.027 for MDM2, and 0.018 for USP7. H170/R134, STK11 loss versus intact for dependency_STAT3, gives a small signed estimate of +0.0145 with a 95% interval from -0.0137 to +0.0427. The point estimate is below the clinically meaningful threshold and the interval crosses both null and the threshold; this does not support a robust STK11-STAT3 association, but it also does not exclude a modest effect. I mark H170 unresolved and close it because further probing of this particular main-effect screen is low priority. H171/R135, ARID1A loss for dependency_STAT3, gives signed -0.0133 with interval -0.0393 to +0.0128. This opposes the registered stronger-dependency direction and the upper bound is below the +0.028 threshold, so a clinically meaningful effect in that registered direction is excluded for the claim as specified; I reject and close H171. H172/R136, RB1 loss for dependency_WRN, gives signed +0.0154 with interval -0.0216 to +0.0525. The point estimate is below the WRN threshold and the interval crosses null and threshold, leaving the evidence insufficient; H172 is unresolved and closed. The remaining twelve-growth and technical-stratum results are strong confirmations of already supported dataset-only associations rather than new independent causal claims. H173/R137, H174/R138, H175/R139, H176/R140, H177/R141, and H178/R142 test low growth-rate contexts for SMARCA4-SMARCA2, MSI-WRN, KEAP1-NFE2L2, TP53-wildtype CDKN2A-MDM2, PTEN-STAT3, and TP53-USP7. All have lower confidence bounds far above their respective 10% benchmarks, so each is accepted and closed as a robustness stratum. H179/R143 tests PTEN loss within PIK3CA-mutant cells for STAT3 dependency and gives signed +0.268 with lower bound +0.127, well above threshold. The effect is biologically and statistically supportive, but the exposed PTEN-loss cell in PIK3CA-mutant samples is small (38 cells), so I accept it as a cautious dataset-only stratum and close it. H180/R144 and H181/R145 test low-Cas9 technical strata for SMARCA4-SMARCA2 and TP53-wildtype CDKN2A-MDM2. Both have large lower bounds above thresholds and are accepted and closed. Overall, this batch supports persistence of the six validated dataset-only associations across slower-growing and lower-Cas9 contexts, while the new main-effect screens for STK11-STAT3 and RB1-WRN remain inconclusive and ARID1A-STAT3 in the registered direction is not supported. These are observational associations in the supplied dataset; conditioning on growth rate or Cas9 activity can introduce collider or technical confounding, and many strata are confirmatory rather than independent validation. No voluntary validation request is made because no new validation requests remain.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 appraise. New low-growth and low-Cas9 strata are strong, internally consistent confirmations of the six validated dataset-only associations, not new independent causal effects. H173/H174/H175/H176/H177/H178 and H180/H181 have lower confidence bounds above their approximate 10% mean-scale thresholds and are accepted closed as dataset-only context robustness. H179 PTEN loss in PIK3CA-mutant cells supports STAT3 with lower bound 0.127, but exposed n=38; accept closed with caution. New main-effect screens H170 STK11-STAT3 and H172 RB1-WRN are insufficient (points below threshold; intervals cross threshold/null) and closed unresolved. H171 ARID1A-STAT3 rejected/closed because signed upper bound below the STAT3 threshold and estimate opposes registered direction. No voluntary validation requested because remaining new requests is zero. Interpret all strata as observational; conditioning on growth/Cas9 may introduce collider/confounding, and many strata are post hoc/confirmatory. Existing active claims remain: H37/H38 SMARCA2 high-Cas9/high-aneuploidy; H60/H61 PTEN lineage; H65 STAT3 IFN; H75/H76 USP7 library; H78/H79 USP7 lineage; H81 SMARCA2 squamous; H90/H103 EGFR KRAS contexts. Prioritize lineage strata for accepted associations; if H90/H103 arrive, interpret as exploratory driver-interaction screens, not accepted."
