atum tests whether the CDKN2A-loss-MDM2 association remains in a proliferative/transcriptionally amplified context. The two new PTEN-loss main-effect claims for POLR2A and RPL11 test a different mechanistic axis: PTEN loss may increase PI3K/AKT/mTOR-associated biosynthetic demand, potentially strengthening dependency on RNA polymerase II and ribosome-biogenesis machinery. The POLR2A MYC-amplification test in low baseline MYC-expression cells tests whether MYC amplification has context-dependent transcriptional effects when baseline MYC mRNA is low; if MYC amplification is buffered or nonfunctional in this setting, the estimate should be near null or opposite. For outcome-scale importance, I will judge signed lower confidence bounds against approximately 10% of the absolute mean dependency score: SMARCA2 about 0.042, WRN about 0.030, STAT3 about 0.028, MDM2 about 0.027, POLR2A about 0.025, RPL11 about 0.025, and lower but still relevant scales for USP7 and NFE2L2. Because no voluntary validation budget remains, newly discovered effects must be judged from discovery uncertainty, cell sizes, consistency with existing accepted effects, and plausibility, with extra caution for new exploratory axes. All conclusions remain observational associations in the supplied dataset only, not causal effects or claims about generalizability."
