  "narrative": "No assessments are due. With the independent validation budget exhausted, I prioritize high-yield discovery refinements rather than broad low-precision effect modification. The main unresolved discovery lead is H90: EGFR amplification among KRAS-mutant cells has a signed estimate of about +0.053 relative to the registered negative dependency direction, but the discovery interval only partly clears the approximate 0.025 EGFR practical benchmark. I therefore register two high-quality technical refinements: KRAS-mutant cells screened with Avana and high Cas9 activity, and KRAS-mutant cells with high screen ROC quality. These are not new biological hypotheses but robustness checks against assay noise; if either gives a signed lower bound above the EGFR benchmark with adequate cell counts, the signal becomes more credible, although it would still be discovery evidence only. I also register low-serum strata for the six accepted main associations: SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2, PTEN-loss/STAT3, TP53-loss/USP7, and CDKN2A-loss-in-TP53-intact/MDM2. High-serum robustness is already partly supported, but low-serum is mechanistically important because nutrient and culture context can alter dependency. I activate the direct squamous SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 stratum H81 because this accepted effect lacks a clean squamous direct estimate, and activate H153 because the adenocarcinoma subset of the EGFR-amplification/KRAS-mutant lead is informative despite prior imprecision. I close or defer lower-priority probes with weak prior evidence or redundant mechanistic axes: H111 MYC/KIF18A is near null, H207 POLR2A/MYC low expression is low priority after MYC biosynthetic effects were weak, and H200, H202, H204 are context probes less essential than completing female, low-serum, and direct-lineage robustness. Research markers D, E, and F remain closed for TMED10 because they are constructed assays without assigned biology and the available discovery budget is better spent on accepted-effects robustness and the EGFR/KRAS lead. All new comparisons retain the accepted direction: for stronger dependency hypotheses, direction -1 expects raw exposed-minus-comparator scores to be more negative; for weaker dependency hypotheses, direction +1 expects raw scores to be less negative. Returned estimates and intervals are already signed, so positive signed values support the registered hypothesis. For interpretation, I will use approximate 10%-of-absolute-mean outcome benchmarks and require consistent direction, adequate cell counts, and interval support before accepting a new stratum as a meaningful dataset-only association.",
