  "narrative": "No discovery assessments are due and the independent-validation budget is exhausted, so this explore stage registers a small, prespecified set of follow-up comparisons rather than broad subgroup fishing. The first six proposals test whether the six core dataset-only associations persist in male cells with adequate Cas9 activity: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, and CDKN2A loss among TP53-intact cells with stronger MDM2 dependency. Male sex is a completed robustness check not yet available for several of these core effects, and restricting to adequate Cas9 activity preserves screen reliability while testing sex-specific internal generalization. These are not new biological mechanisms; they are complementary internal replication strata. Expected raw exposed-minus-comparator contrasts are negative for stronger-dependency claims under direction -1 and positive for weaker-dependency claims under direction +1; controller estimates will already be signed to the registered direction and should not be re-signed. If all remain above practical thresholds, this strengthens the conclusion that the core associations are not sex- or editing-specific in this dataset; if unresolved, it only means inadequate evidence in that narrower stratum, not absence of an effect.\n\nThe next two proposals test whether the accepted STK11-loss association with stronger USP7 dependency is modified by TP53 status. This is biologically prioritized because USP7 is closely linked to p53 pathway biology: if STK11-loss dependency on USP7 is substantially different between TP53-intact and TP53-loss cells, that would indicate a p53-dependent context; if both strata remain strong and similar, the simpler STK11 main association is more defensible. The anticipated raw direction in both conditionals is negative because each hypothesis is that STK11-loss cells have stronger USP7 dependency. Practical benchmark for USP7 is roughly 0.018 absolute dependency-score units. These tests can add conditional precision without launching broad co-alteration fishing.\n\nThe final proposal is a narrow, mechanistically motivated new hypothesis: BRCA2 loss may be associated with stronger KIF18A dependency. BRCA2 deficiency produces mitotic chromosomal-segregation defects, and KIF18A is a mitotic regulator; this makes a specific falsifiable prediction rather than an arbitrary predictor-outcome pair. The expected raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative under direction -1. A strong clinically meaningful effect would exceed the approximate 10% benchmark for KIF18A dependency, roughly 0.026 absolute units. The plausible alternatives are a trivial/null effect or a nonmeaningful small effect, which would leave KIF18A without a measured biomarker in this dataset. These proposals are all dataset-only association tests and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Explore stage plan: validate the six core dataset-only associations in male + adequate-Cas9 strata, then probe STK11-loss USP7 effects within TP53-intact and TP53-loss strata, and test one mechanistically motivated BRCA2-loss/KIF18A-dependency hypothesis. Avoid broad subgroup fishing and small co-alteration cells unless cell counts are adequate. Interpret controller estimates as already signed to registered hypothesis directions. For direction -1 stronger-dependency claims, raw contrasts are expected negative; for direction +1 weaker-dependency claims, raw contrasts are expected positive. Practical benchmarks remain approximate 10% absolute-mean outcome scales: SMARCA2 about 0.042, WRN about 0.030, STAT3 about 0.028, USP7 about 0.018, MDM2 about 0.027, NFE2L2 about 0.009, and KIF18A about 0.026. Acceptance requires not only statistical evidence but lower bounds or stable estimates far above these practical scales. If male+Cas9 core strata remain accepted, treat them as additional internal robustness only. For STK11/USP7, prefer a coherent pattern across TP53 strata over isolated interaction claims. If BRCA2/KIF18A is null or below practical threshold, do not overinterpret; many non-driver dependencies appear generic or weakly associated in this dataset."
